# Pester Tests

Pester 5.x. Run full suite: `./test.sh` (WSL) or `.\test.ps1` (Windows).

## Structure

```powershell
BeforeAll {
    $script:Root = Split-Path $PSScriptRoot -Parent
    $script:Fixtures = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'fixtures'
    . (Join-Path $script:Root 'lib\LogParser.ps1')  # or relevant loader
}
```

## Fixtures

- Place logs in `tests/fixtures/<descriptive-name>.log`
- Every new parser pattern needs a fixture + `It` block in `LogParser.Tests.ps1`
- Real logs: copy from exam PC `%temp%\inspera-launcher-*.log`; sanitize if needed

## Test files

| File | Focus |
|---|---|
| `LogParser.Tests.ps1` | Parsing, failure detection, log discovery |
| `ProcessManager.Tests.ps1` | Blocklist merge, dry-run cleanup |
| `SystemChecks.Tests.ps1` | Environment audit, targeted check mapping |
| `Smoke.Tests.ps1` | End-to-end entry scripts |
| `AppRoot.Tests.ps1` | `Get-InsperaAppRoot` / `Get-InsperaRoot` |

Filter: `./test.sh -Filter 'Parse-InsperaLog'`
